[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2126969690","pull_request_review_id":2897339337,"id":2126969690,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5-xvta","diff_hunk":"@@ -700,7 +700,7 @@ void RasterizerSceneGLES3::_setup_sky(const RenderDataGLES3 *p_render_data, cons\n \t\t\t\t\tsky_light_data.energy *= RSG::camera_attributes->camera_attributes_get_exposure_normalization_factor(p_render_data->camera_attributes);\n \t\t\t\t}\n \n-\t\t\t\tColor linear_col = light_storage->light_get_color(base);\n+\t\t\t\tColor linear_col = light_storage->light_get_color(base).srgb_to_linear();","path":"drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp","commit_id":"bac9427325a919ccb2a1b1e3934465db24a67eb8","original_commit_id":"d388ecd1545eebfbcc66c082ac6160ce15da6c5d","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Great catch!\r\n\r\nHowever, this is slightly the wrong approach. It affects the appearance of the sun in the sky shader. \r\n\r\n_With this PR, compatibility_\r\n<img width=\"619\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-06-04 at 8 17 43 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/281f97e6-6dc0-4a4d-8f6c-b6d0ccc7c7a4\" />\r\n\r\n_Forward+_\r\n<img width=\"578\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-06-04 at 8 20 13 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f047b9f-6372-4066-83c7-f36df345fc0a\" />\r\n\r\nThe problem comes from how we handle sRGB space in sky shaders. In general the compatibility renderer uses sRGB space for everything except for direct lighting. I.e. all the inputs to the shader are sRGB, inside the shader they get converted to linear for direct lighting then back to sRGB. \r\n\r\nTherefore in the scene shader, we can just pass the light colors in linear. \r\n\r\nIn sky shaders, fog is calculated in linear space, but the rest of the sky is in sRGB space. Since we expose the light_color value directly to users, we need to either convert the light color to linear manually in the shader when calculating fog, or we need to pass in linear color separately. ","created_at":"2025-06-04T16:09:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T16:09:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107099#discussion_r2126969690","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107099","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2126969690"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107099#discussion_r2126969690"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107099"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2126969690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":703,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2127506724","pull_request_review_id":2898211484,"id":2127506724,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5-zy0k","diff_hunk":"@@ -700,7 +700,7 @@ void RasterizerSceneGLES3::_setup_sky(const RenderDataGLES3 *p_render_data, cons\n \t\t\t\t\tsky_light_data.energy *= RSG::camera_attributes->camera_attributes_get_exposure_normalization_factor(p_render_data->camera_attributes);\n \t\t\t\t}\n \n-\t\t\t\tColor linear_col = light_storage->light_get_color(base);\n+\t\t\t\tColor linear_col = light_storage->light_get_color(base).srgb_to_linear();","path":"drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp","commit_id":"bac9427325a919ccb2a1b1e3934465db24a67eb8","original_commit_id":"d388ecd1545eebfbcc66c082ac6160ce15da6c5d","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@clayjohn I tested master, this pr before changing it as you suggested, as well as after and they all have this problem with the sun colour being different in Compatibility than in Forward+. Changing this value actually didn't seem to affect the sun from my testing. I changed it though to do the sRGB -> linear conversion in the shader because as you noted, the light_color value is exposed in users' shaders.","created_at":"2025-06-04T21:53:29Z","updat